# Insurance

Wizard step 7 (Conversion is 8). Policies live in `household.insurance`
(one list, `kind` = `life` | `disability` | `longTermCare`, soft-deleted to
`deletedInsurance`). `migrateHousehold` heals every field.

**A policy only pays in its own analysis.** Retirement never reads
`household.insurance`; `insurance.test.ts` pins that `calculate()` is
identical with or without policies. Premiums and cash value are stored for
reference only (not expenses, not assets).

## Life insurance summary
`LifeInsuranceSummary` (top of the Life section) is one table grouped by
insured, built by `lifeInsuranceSummary(household, year)`: type, coverage,
face, cash value, premium / yr, and the survivor income a death this year
would pay. Ended term policies are listed greyed out and left out of the
per-insured and household totals.

## Life (Survivorship)
- In force: permanent always; term from `issueYear` for `termYears`.
- On the insured's death (end of `death.year`), the face amount lands that
  same year as `balances["life:<id>"]` (inside `afterTaxTotal`, so totals and
  inheritance include it). From the next year it grows 8% a year
  (`LIFE_INSURANCE_PROCEEDS_GROWTH`), and pays a fixed lifetime income of
  face x rate (`incomeMonthly["life:<id>"]`), even if the balance runs out.
- Rate: Transamerica RILA Income Advantage with Step-Up, Single Life,
  "Immediate Payout %" by the insured's age at death
  (`config/lifeInsurancePayout.ts`). Under 59: 5%. Past 86: the 86 rate.
- Tax: annuity LIFO. Earnings (balance over remaining basis) come out first
  as ordinary income; the rest returns basis tax free.

## Disability (Disability analysis)
- Occupation definition is descriptive only.
- Pays `monthlyBenefit` for months [waiting, end) counted from January 1 of
  the disability year. Waiting 30/60/90/180 days = 1/2/3/6 months, 365 = 12,
  730 = 24. End: 2/5/10 years after the wait, or January 1 of the year the
  insured turns 65 / 67. Key `di:<id>`. Tax free unless `taxable`.

## Long-term care (Long-term care analysis)
- For each care stay of the insured: pays min(benefit, that year's care
  cost) per month after the waiting period, for `benefitYears` (or
  lifetime), never past the stay. Key `ltci:<id>`, tax free.
- Doesn't change the expense rules (70% / 0%) in the analyses guide.

## Colors in the Assets, Income & Taxes tables
`SnapshotLine.tint` gives lines their own row color (`TINT_ROW` in
`ScenarioSnapshot.tsx`): life (proceeds and income) teal, disability peach,
long-term care insurance mauve, real estate tan, business lavender.
